This section is part of my JavaScript self-learning journey.
I learned the basic tools and concepts needed to start building web pages with HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.

📚 Topics Learned

13. VS Code IDE

Learned the basics of using Visual Studio Code (VS Code) as a code editor for web development.

Covered:

Creating and managing files

Writing and editing code

Working with folders and projects

Using the integrated terminal

Running and testing code

Basic editor features useful for development

14. HTML Tags – Introduction

Learned the basics of HTML (HyperText Markup Language) and how HTML tags are used to structure web pages.

Covered introductory tags such as:

Headings: <h1> to <h6>

Paragraph: <p>

Links: <a>

Images: <img>

Lists: <ul>, <ol>, <li>

Basic document structure

15. CSS – Introduction

Learned the basics of CSS (Cascading Style Sheets) and how it is used to style HTML elements.

Covered:

Applying CSS to HTML

Basic selectors

Colors

Fonts and text styling

Backgrounds

Basic spacing and styling concepts

16. Query Selector

Learned how JavaScript can select HTML elements from the DOM using querySelector().

Example:

const heading = document.querySelector("h1");

Also understood that CSS-style selectors can be used to target elements.

17. <script> Tag

Learned how JavaScript is connected to an HTML page using the <script> tag.

Example:

<script src="script.js"></script>

This allows JavaScript code to interact with and add behavior to a web page.

18. Comments

Learned how to write comments in JavaScript to make code easier to understand and maintain.

Single-line comment:

// This is a comment

Multi-line comment:

/*
   This is a
   multi-line comment
*/

